 "state_profile": {
  "voting_summary": "Alaska offers no-excuse absentee voting and 15 days of early in-person voting, but about half of its 2024 vote was still cast on election day. Polls close at 12 a.m. Eastern, and only election day and early in-person votes report on election night. Absentee ballots may arrive up to 10 days after election day (15 for overseas), and the state counts them in batches over the following two weeks, with final unofficial results around day 15. Mail ran D+7 against R+20 on election day, so Alaska drifts steadily bluer after election night before ranked-choice tabulation settles any race without a majority.",
